 "answer": "The environment variable that changes where Ollama stores downloaded models on Windows is `OLLAMA_MODELS`. According to the context provided in the project's documents, you can set this environment variable to specify a different directory for storing the models. Here's how you can do it on Windows:\n\n1. Quit the Ollama application if it is running.\n2. Open the Settings application (Windows 11) or Control Panel (Windows 10) and search for \"environment variables.\"\n3. Click on \"Edit environment variables for your account.\"\n4. Edit or create a new user account variable named `OLLAMA_MODELS` and set it to your desired directory path.\n5. Click OK/Apply to save your changes.\n\nAfter setting this environment variable, if Ollama is already running, you should quit the application and relaunch it to apply the changes.",
